vectors.json: ground truth for muster's LEZ v0.2.4 public-transaction encoder (lez/tx.nim).

It was generated by generator/, a Rust program built against LEZ's own crates and
lez-multisig's instruction type:
- lee, lee_core and common from logos-blockchain/logos-execution-zone @ v0.2.4;
- token_core from the same repo, for the token-program instruction words;
- multisig_core from logos-co/lez-multisig, branch feat/lee-v0.2.4 (PR #45). That is the
  program deployed on the testnet as ImageID 2ced3d30…d4c7.

Regenerate it with the generator's Cargo.lock (the lez-multisig lock). The build needs the
same system libraries as the LEZ wallet; see docs/labbook/lez-multisig-versions.md.

  cd generator && RISC0_SKIP_BUILD=1 cargo +1.94.0 run -q > ../vectors.json

What it pins:
- keys: account id = SHA-256("/LEE/v0.3/AccountId/Public/" padded ‖ BIP-340 x-only key).
- instructions: multisig_core::Instruction through Program::serialize_instruction, i.e.
  risc0 serde words: a byte is one word, a u64 two, a u128 four, a Vec its length then its
  items, an enum its variant index.
- txs: Message borsh, Message::hash, BIP-340 signatures, PublicTransaction borsh + hash,
  and LeeTransaction::Public borsh in base64 (what sendTransaction takes).
  - The signatures use 32 zero bytes of aux randomness (k256 sign_prehash_with_aux_rand),
    so they are deterministic.
  - WitnessSet::is_valid_for is asserted before output.
- deploy: LeeTransaction::ProgramDeployment for a 5-byte stand-in bytecode, and its hash.
- token: the token program's instruction words for the live e2e (NewFungibleDefinition
  "MusterTest" 1_000_000, InitializeAccount, Transfer 500 / 200).

The account ids in txs (0xa1…, 0xa2…) are stand-ins; the PDAs themselves are held to real
chain bytes in vectors/lez-multisig-{v024,testnet}. Generated 2026-09-25.
